  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1257 PM MDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nFor the San JUan mtns (SJU mtns)...\n\nA deep trough is fcst to form over the western CONUS and then move \nslowly east through mid to late week. This trough will draw up \ntropical moisture into the SJU mtn. Given this...\n\nScattered showers are expected during the Tuesday time frame. \nWednesday will likely see little if any precip SJU mtns, but the \nprecip will ramp up Wednesday evening and last into Friday. The \nprecip will likely be heavy as a review of the guidance shows a \ndirect moisture tap coming into the sju mtns. Statistical products \n(NBM 1 viewer) are showing 2-3\" of liquid with this first round of \nprecip. Since this moisture source is coming directly into the \nregion from the subtropics, it will be warm and most, if not all, of \nthe precip will be rain.\n\nA second round of lift will move over the SJU mtns from late Sunday \nthrough Monday. This forcing will be more associated with the mid \nlevel 500 mb trough, and temps will be colder. This will allow for \nthe precip to have a bit more snow with it, and another inch or so \nof liquid equivalent will be possible.\n\nAs has been mentioned in several previous AFDs, The SJU mtn region \nis soaked and any additional heavy precip is likely going to cause \nhigh water issues. Additionally, looking at visible sat pix imagery, \nthere appears to be quite a bit of fresh snow in place over the \nhigher peaks of the SJU mtns, and the upcoming heavy rain combined \nwith snow melt could make the high water issues worse. Folks who \nlive in the region OR are traveling in this region are strongly urged \nto pay attention to later forecast regarding this upcoming weather \nsituation. All the typical hazards associated with heavy rain in the \nmtns will be possible (rock slides/flash flooding) \n\n\nFor the plains...\n\nDry and warm through Thursday. Warm weather continues into Friday, \nbut we may see some showers over the lower elevations, especially \nalong the NM border and the KS border areas. It will be cooler all \nof plains Saturday and Sunday with a chance of showers, once again \nbest chances will be along the NM and KS borders.\n\n\nValleys, central mtns and mtns adjacent to plains...\n\nisolate precip Tues with somewhat drier Wednesday during the \ndaylight hours, but shower will pick up Wednesday evening into \nFriday, especially over the central mtns, valleys and west slopes of \nthe mtns adjacent to the plains. Precip will be more scattered late \nFriday into the weekend. \\/Hodanish",
